      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "At that instant, is the total surface area of the cylinder, including its two circular ends, increasing or decreasing? Justify your answer.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\frac{dT}{dt} = \\frac{14\\pi}{5} > 0, \\; \\text{increasing}",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Total surface area is the curved side plus the two ends.",
               "latex": "T = 2\\pi r L + 2\\pi r^{2}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Differentiate with respect to t.",
               "latex": "\\frac{dT}{dt} = \\frac{dS}{dt} + 4\\pi r\\frac{dr}{dt}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Substitute the values at that instant.",
               "latex": "\\frac{dT}{dt} = \\frac{18\\pi}{5} + 4\\pi(2)(-0.1) = \\frac{14\\pi}{5}"
            },
            {
               "text": "The rate is positive, so the total surface area is increasing.",
               "latex": "\\frac{dT}{dt} > 0"
            }
         ],
